        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Hantavirus outbreak: US, French nationals test positive after evacuating ship Issued on: 11/05/2026 - 12:49 An American citizen and a French woman evacuated from the cruise ship hit by a deadly hantavirus outbreak have tested positive, officials said, as the repatriation operation continued on Monday. Following the positive test results, Spain defended the rigour of its sanitary measures during the complex evacuation Sunday of 94 people of 19 different nationalities from the MV Hondius, which is moored in the Canary Islands. FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin reports from Bichat Hospital in central Paris. Suspected hantavirus case triggers emergency deployment to isolated island 11/05/2026 Iran Nobel winner Narges Mohammadi released on bail for medical treatment 11/05/2026 Russia, China and Iran: What do Beijing and Moscow want to gain from conflict? 11/05/2026 French passenger from hantavirus ship tests positive 11/05/2026 Hantavirus: Ship evacuations enter second day 11/05/2026 Health REPLAY: Under-pressure UK PM addresses nation after election losses 11/05/2026 Eurovision fever hits host city Vienna 11/05/2026 Hantavirus outbreak renews painful memories for Patagonian village 11/05/2026 US-Israel war on Iran: Hormuz island tourism takes a hit 11/05/2026"
