        "contenuto_esteso": "Advertisement Britain World Europe Under-threat UK PM Starmer vows to prove ‘doubters’ wrong Starmer has failed to spur economic growth and has swerved from one policy misstep to another 3 -MIN READ 3 -MIN Listen Agence France-Presse Published: 6:45pm, 11 May 2026 Embattled British Prime Minister Keir Starmer vowed on Monday to prove his “doubters” wrong, as he sought to quell a growing threat to his leadership following disastrous local and regional polls. Starmer pledged his ruling Labour party would do “better” as he tried to convince angry and restless lawmakers to back him in a crunch speech designed to reset his flagging premiership. “I know that people are frustrated by the state of Britain, frustrated by politics, and some people frustrated with me,” he said during an address in central London. Advertisement “I know I have my doubters, and I know I need to prove them wrong, and I will,” added Starmer, who returned Labour to power after 14 years of Conservative rule in 2024. Starmer has swerved from one policy misstep to another since then, and is engulfed in a scandal over the appointment – and sacking – of Peter Mandelson as UK ambassador to Washington, after revelations about the envoy’s ties to the sex offender Jeffrey Epstein. Advertisement The prime minister has failed to spur economic growth as British citizens continue to feel the effects of a years-long cost-of-living pinch, but has been praised for resisting US President Donald Trump over Iran. Advertisement Select Voice Select Speed 00:00 00:00 1.00"
